content.thinking:
Python -c requires approval. Let me try simpler grep-based approach with individual commands. I can extract "MACRO pin DIRECTION" triples with awk but as a single awk command per file, redirecting to /tmp. Writing to /tmp — is that allowed? The rule says I can only WRITE files into the tutorial dir. Hmm, strictly, "你可以写文件，但只能写入 icsprout55-pdk-tutorial/". Redirecting temp analysis files to /tmp violates the letter of that rule. But grep pipelines to stdout are fine.

Alternative: single awk command reading BOTH files in one invocation, no temp files. One awk process, print direction triples per file with FILENAME, then... I need to diff. I can do it all in one awk: store dir per (FILENAME,macro,pin), and at END compare. Let me write one awk program that processes both files.

awk '
/^MACRO /{m=$2}
/^  PIN /{p=$2}
/DIRECTION/{d[FILENAME SUBSEP m SUBSEP p]=$2; keys[FILENAME SUBSEP m SUBSEP p]=1; mf[m]=1}
END { ... compare for macros ... }
' file1 file2

In END, for each macro in mf, for each key of file1, compare with file2. Keys: I stored with SUBSEP. I can iterate over keys of file1, split, and check file2.

Let me construct it carefully. Note FILENAME is available. Output: print macro pin dir1 dir2 when differ. Also count macros with different pin sets — harder; skip, we know PIN counts are equal (5069 each) and the earlier per-file counts matched, plus git diff e5c881b only changed DIRECTION lines. Actually pin SETS: since only DIRECTION lines changed in e5c881b for ecos (relative to earlier ecos), but between norm and ecos there could still be pin set differences... The counts: PIN lines 5069 both; VDD/VSS 785+785 both. Signal pins = 5069-1570=3499. And MET2 count in ecos = 3499 = exactly the number of signal pins! So every signal pin got exactly ONE MET2 rect and ONE VIA1 rect.

That's a beautiful quantitative finding: 3499 signal pins ↔ 3499 LAYER MET2 ↔ 3499 LAYER VIA1.

Now the awk for direction diffs. Keep it as ONE awk invocation (single operation, no &&, no redirects).

